{
  "_comment": [
    "Open-shell CCSD(T) reference energies for the native OpenQP path.",
    "Generated with PySCF on the same geometry and basis, then reproduced end to",
    "end through OpenQP's own integral engine and the spin-orbital solver.",
    "",
    "scf_type selects the reference. UHF is canonical, so its f_ov vanishes.",
    "ROHF is not: semicanonicalisation leaves the occupied-virtual Fock block,",
    "and both the amplitude equations and the correlation energy need it.",
    "",
    "triples_tolerance is per case and deliberately loose for ROHF. (T) is not",
    "invariant to occ-occ and vir-vir rotations, so it depends on the orbital",
    "basis in a way CCSD does not; this code evaluates it semicanonically and",
    "PySCF does not. The residual tracks open-shell character (6e-12 on a",
    "closed-shell ROHF case, 4e-7 on a triplet). That is a convention",
    "difference, not agreement, so the tolerance says so instead of hiding it.",
    "",
    "cartesian=true throughout: OpenQP uses 6d Cartesian shells, so PySCF needs",
    "gto.M(..., cart=True) or the two codes run different basis sets.",
    "",
    "The fzc1 ROHF cases cover frozen core on a non-canonical reference. The",
    "frozen orbitals have to be taken out BEFORE semicanonicalisation: the",
    "occupied rotation mixes core with valence, and alpha and beta rotate",
    "separately, so freezing afterwards correlates a different space in each",
    "spin. Doing it in the wrong order still converges and still looks",
    "plausible -- it was off by 4e-7 to 9e-6 Hartree, which is why these cases",
    "exist."
  ],
